      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "BTS — FAKE LOVE",
      "content": "Concession. \"Even if you leave, I'll be okay.\"\n\nThe title track from Love Yourself: Tear (2018), the album that pushed BTS's 'Love Yourself' series toward its darkest point. The whole Love Yourself arc is about learning to love yourself before you can love anyone else — and FAKE LOVE is the moment that lesson gets learned the hard way.\n\nIn this lesson, you'll learn the grammar pattern **-아/어도**, which means \"even though, even if.\" We'll see how BTS uses it in \"FAKE LOVE.\"",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "label": null,
      "title": "이번에 배울 것",
      "content": "이번 레슨에서 배울 단어:\n- **사라지다** — to disappear\n- **곁** — side (of a person)\n- **사라져도** — even if (you) disappear\n- **아파도 괜찮다** — even if it hurts, it's okay\n\n레슨이 끝나면, 이 노래의 가사를 이해할 수 있어요.",
      "musicPlaying": true
    },
